gHTddtkgVFDk4_62Y4NaSwTzaeMJVNiPTc4B85Mrq4=", "uri": "https://mediagateway.sweet.io/media/token/Pbd44mbK/12167600293248237568/poster-image-square.png"}], "reverse_image": null}, "attributes": [{"name": "Audio Type", "value": "Sounds of the Game"}, {"name": "Crafted from Editions", "value": "498,485,464,274,213,170,193,420,98"}, {"name": "Crafted from Rarity", "value": "Limited"}, {"name": "Date", "value": "2023-04-05"}, {"name": "Edition Number", "value": "1"}, {"name": "Moment UUID", "value": "b5c8ae779c380000a8dc000000000000"}, {"name": "Play", "value": "Save"}, {"name": "Player", "value": "Jacob Markstrom"}, {"name": "Rarity", "value": "Heroic"}, {"name": "Series", "value": "Series 1"}, {"name": "Series UUID", "value": "b5c8ae77000000000000000000000000"}, {"name": "Set", "value": "Signature Limiteds"}, {"name": "Set UUID", "value": "b5c8ae779c3800000000000000000000"}, {"name": "Team", "value": "Calgary Flames"}], "creator": {"name": "SocialSweet Inc.", "uri": "https://sweet.io"}, "description": "As the 2022-23 season was drawing to a close, the Calgary Flames and Winnipeg Jets found themselves in a fierce battle for the final playoff spot. In a crucial matchup between the two teams, Jacob Markstrom rose to the occasion in what felt like a must-win game, turning aside 34 of 35 shots for Calgary. During the second period, with the Jets holding a 1-0 lead, Markstrom made a pivotal stop on Pierre-Luc Dubois' doorstep attempt just before Calgary stormed down the ice to tie the game. Later in the same period, with the score level, he showcased his skills by blocking a blistering Mark Scheifele slap shot and then diving to thwart Josh Morrissey's rebound effort. In the final two minutes of the game, Markstrom preserved Calgary's two-goal lead by denying Nikolaj Ehlers on a breakaway attempt. Markstrom's exceptional performance rightfully earned him the first star of the game honors in this high-stakes matchup.\r\n\r\nOfficially Licensed Product of the NHL, NHLPA, and/or